{%- comment -%}
  LBASS — GUIDES BRANCH FOR THE MAIN MENU (2026-08-03)
  Rendered from snippets/lbass-menu.liquid, inside .lbm-list.

  WHY IT EXISTS
  Audited 2026-08-03 on the live site: the store had TEN published Darija
  guides and exactly ONE link to any of them anywhere in the site chrome (the
  footer entity block). `.lb-catnav` and `header.top` are both display:none —
  hidden by lbass-menu.liquid — so the side panel IS the navigation, and it
  had no path to the blog at all.

  Ten pages of crawlable Darija content that nothing links to are, for ranking
  purposes, close to invisible: no internal PageRank flows to them and a
  crawler reaches them only via the sitemap. This puts every article one click
  from every page on the site.

  DYNAMIC ON PURPOSE
  Reads blogs['news'].articles, so publishing article 11 adds it here with no
  code change, and an empty blog prints nothing rather than a dead branch.

  Kept in its own file because lbass-menu.liquid is already ~19KB; folding this
  in would make that file harder to reason about, and the guides list is the
  part most likely to change.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign lb_blog = blogs['news'] -%}
{%- comment -%}
  MERGED 2026-09-01 (owner request). This snippet used to emit TWO top-level menu
  items — "أدلة" (blog) and "أدلة الشراء" (pSEO pages). The top level is now capped
  at five entries: رجال · نساء · جديد · البراندات · أدلة. Everything secondary —
  buying guides, blog, بدا من هنا, قطع 1/1, Vault — lives inside this ONE أدلة item.
  NOTE: {% render %} is an isolated scope, so collections are looked up here again;
  variables assigned in lbass-menu.liquid are NOT visible inside this snippet.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  ═══ SECOND BRANCH: THE pSEO / QUERY-FIRST PAGES (added 2026-08-23) ═══

  The branch above covers blog ARTICLES. It never covered the query-first
  PAGES, and a link-graph crawl of all 120 indexable URLs on 2026-08-23 found
  these receiving ZERO inbound internal links from anywhere on the site:

      /pages/adidas-second-hand-maroc          0 inbound
      /pages/jordan-second-hand-maroc          0
      /pages/cargo-pants-second-hand-maroc     0
      /pages/jackets-second-hand-maroc         0
      /pages/streetwear-original-maroc         0
      /pages/comment-acheter-second-hand-…     0
      /pages/ma3na-thrift-second-hand-…        0

  plus two money pages that were close to it:
      /pages/vetements-second-hand-maroc       3 inbound
      /pages/sneakers-second-hand-maroc       11 inbound
  against 114–115 for comparable pages that sit in the site chrome.

  They were written, indexed and left unreachable — no internal PageRank, and
  a crawler finds them only through the sitemap. This puts each one click from
  every page, which is what the other query-first pages already get.

  /collections/frontpage is deliberately NOT here: it serves noindex.

  LOOKED UP THROUGH `pages[handle]`, NOT HARDCODED <a href>. If a page is ever
  unpublished or renamed, the guard drops the row instead of shipping a dead
  internal link — the failure mode this file exists to prevent.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%}
  how-we-check-items leads deliberately. It was BUILT (a complete 14KB template,
  templates/page.how-we-check.liquid, with FAQPage + AboutPage schema) and then
  never shipped — the page record sat unpublished, with an empty body, pointing
  at the wrong template suffix. Published 2026-08-23. It is the only page that
  answers "how do clothes get from Germany to Morocco" end to end, which was
  logged as a MISSING asset in the implementation audit.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign lb_guide_handles = 'how-we-check-items,ma3na-thrift-second-hand-vintage-one-of-one,sneakers-second-hand-maroc,vetements-second-hand-maroc,adidas-second-hand-maroc,nike-second-hand-maroc,jordan-second-hand-maroc,jackets-second-hand-maroc,cargo-pants-second-hand-maroc,streetwear-original-maroc,comment-acheter-second-hand-original-maroc' | split: ',' -%}
{%- capture lb_guide_rows -%}
  {%- for gh in lb_guide_handles -%}
    {%- assign gp = pages[gh] -%}
    {%- if gp.handle != blank -%}
      <li><a href="{{ gp.url }}">{{ gp.title }}</a></li>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endcapture -%}
{%- assign lb_oneofone = collections['one-of-one'] -%}
{%- assign lb_oo_count = lb_oneofone.products_count | default: 0 | plus: 0 -%}
<li class="lbm-item">
  <button type="button" class="lbm-a lbm-util lbm-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="lbmSubGuides">أدلة<span class="lbm-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
  <ul class="lbm-sub" id="lbmSubGuides" hidden>
    {%- if pages['start-here'] != blank -%}
      <li><a href="{{ pages['start-here'].url }}">أول طلب؟ بدا من هنا</a></li>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if lb_oo_count > 0 -%}
      <li><a href="{{ lb_oneofone.url }}">قطع 1/1 <em>{{ lb_oo_count }}</em></a></li>
    {%- endif -%}
    <li><a href="/pages/vault">Vault</a></li>
    {{ lb_guide_rows }}
    {%- if lb_blog.articles_count > 0 -%}
      {%- for a in lb_blog.articles limit: 6 -%}
        <li><a href="{{ a.url }}">{{ a.title }}</a></li>
      {%- endfor -%}
      <li><a class="lbm-all" href="{{ lb_blog.url }}">شوف كل الأدلة <em>{{ lb_blog.articles_count }}</em></a></li>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Support links moved in here 2026-09-01 (owner request). They used to sit in
      .lbm-foot as a separate always-visible list; the top level is capped at five
      entries, so everything secondary lives under أدلة.
    {%- endcomment -%}
